  "scope": "Independent mathematical and literal-source review of all LGS1-LGS13: integral sandwich, exact exponents and prime bounds, canonical mean, served-coordinate product estimates, full first growth, auxiliary zeroCh, twelve-field admission, and all five original LinkG fields. Actual common compatibility and selected TopsF/Adm2F remain explicit.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "topic": "Integral models and every coefficient place",
      "result": "PASS after precision correction",
      "detail": "Primitive polynomial normalization and both parity weights match IW3. Signed determinant transport does not rescale one lattice separately. For dominant weights absent presenting bases give an empty intersection equal to the ambient model; the separate function space requires zero off lattice tuples. Genuine nondominant coefficient fibers are zero. The exact wExp, tensor multiplicity sum n_v=f, and ep=ceil(Ce*f*k^2*log_p a) give the original sandwich even for p>a."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Actual Frobenius and power bands",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "GandSk supplies the cyclotomic/dyadic reading of the actual hP before the finite order estimate. The exponent arithmetic 1/4+2/3+1/50=281/300 is correct. The power-band integer count retains its endpoint term at width zero. Coefficients precede the family, and thresholds precede members, places, coefficient extensions and degrees."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Local certificates and canonical mean",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The local polynomial rank is k-1, distinct from global m. The integer-certificate attainment in GJ1 justifies the universal canonical infimum. GJ3/GJ4 and BC transport give actual t=ceil(tv), Dp, kappa and cstar=8(Dp+1). Both MeanKappaBound clauses retain their original quantifiers, including every-degree small-prime bounds."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Joint exceptions and first-growth length",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The midpoint pairing cancels w^(-A)*p^A*w^(-A), also for negative A. Integral tests give good Smith directions; tensors survive only when every selected coordinate is bad. Finite free orbit sections give the product count. The walk retains m^(beta+1), every m(t_v+Dp+1), and ep. Smith tails give exactly vO(p)*G.d*(tauP+ioP), with Sv and tauP already integral. Empty service and S=0 are handled. Saturation gives the precise inclusion and quotient injection."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Auxiliary zero chain and original geometric data",
      "result": "PASS after boundary clarification",
      "detail": "Chain has only linear maps, and m>=2, so zeroCh proves every vKge threshold, including negative real ones. LatTied, yProd, NP, Vram, LatDefs, normalized lengths, numerical parameters and LinkG do not use Ch. Extra.ker does use the original geometric chain: LGS11 explicitly retains that record and does not transfer ker or assert a new theta-map valuation. The source zeroCh/linkG_without_kernels interface matches."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Full admission and same-family installer",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "All twelve admitted fields are supplied with C31=Corb, Ce=1, Cm=302114 before delta; all three TypePrimeSizeConds fields are present. All five LinkG_at conclusions retain losses, rank and ramification normalization. The Closed-class bound preserves pre/t/mid/last choice order. Actual GroupCompatibilityFamily and selected TopsF or Adm2F remain explicit; no construction or whole-leaf closure is inferred."
    }
  ],
